00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:23,280
It wasn't always weekly, right?

212
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:27,600
But then I guess in that year, I released three or four new apps overall.

213
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:49,920
I actually had one big app called RedPoint, which is a climbing fitness tracker for Apple Watch, which was my main project back then because it was like a nice niche app, you know, there's no competition because making a climbing app for Apple Watch only is like kind of like yeah, it can maybe sustain half a developer, but that's it.

214
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,480
It's not getting VC funded competition.

215
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:53,600
Exactly.

216
00:18:53,920 --> 00:19:00,640
I was young and I was living in Berlin in a shared apartment, so I was very happy with my situation.

217
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:04,960
But still, I was of course exploring new ideas and one of them was OneSec.

218
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:12,560
And when I released it, it was kind of like every other app that I made where I was like, okay, maybe this will get like...

219
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:15,360
You'll get, I don't know, 100 people or so in the first week.

220
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:17,760
And the story was what you said earlier.

221
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:24,080
It was basically like, you don't like how you're being sucked into social media, but you don't want to completely get rid of it.

222
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:26,080
Like, a lot of people just try to go cold turkey.

223
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:35,120
So you're like, oh, there's APIs that Apple has that lets you jack in basically to when somebody's opening an app, and you can kind of interrupt it.

224
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,360
And that was the kind of driver for why you made it.

225
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,600
But it wasn't like, I'm going to build this big company on this idea.

