00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:14,640
Was a lot of that just organic, you know, the product market fit, you just are watching that thing climb, or were you starting to like, I know now you do lots of different marketing things.

276
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:17,680
Were you doing that back then to try and grow it up to this point?

277
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:24,800
Back then, I think the initial growth really came from my tweet, because that lasted like a long time.

278
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,600
There were always like phases where suddenly it would get more...

279
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,360
The same original tweet.

280
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,280
Yes, the same original tweet.

281
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:31,440
Wow.

282
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:32,000
That's kind of...

283
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:34,000
And it brought me quite far.

284
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:39,600
And then actually at some point, I started to pay for it to be shown to even more people.

285
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:40,000
Yeah.

286
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:41,840
Yeah, because you know it's effective.

287
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,040
Exactly.

288
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:46,080
It kind of like has proven itself that it works organically.

289
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,040
And yeah, that really worked well.

290
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:52,080
That was also actually before Elon Musk took over Twitter.

291
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:54,480
So I was more happy to pay money for it to them.

292
00:24:54,800 --> 00:24:56,480
Nowadays I don't do that anymore.

293
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,000
Did you try replicating that?

294
00:24:58,160 --> 00:25:02,320
Like, were you making more videos, but it was just that original one that was really working?

295
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:12,640
At some point I did a new version of that tweet that was like more polished and it also worked really well, but I kind of like knew.

296
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:36,240
that it would work back then because it was like not changing everything about the original tweet, it was just like making it just a bit more polished and making the wording a bit nicer to explain what the app is doing and putting like an app store link in there with a campaign parameter that I can actually track the traffic coming from there, like stuff like that.

297
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:39,600
And then I also put it out in a couple of different languages at some point.

298
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:41,920
The original was in English, I'm presuming?

299
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:42,160
Yeah.

300
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:43,360
Yeah, exactly.

301
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:44,560
Interesting.

302
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:45,520
So, okay.

303
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:51,600
I mean, really, it sounds like product market fit is kind of the thing that was driving that early growth then.

304
00:25:52,160 --> 00:26:01,200
Like the tweet itself was really effective, but the reason it was effective was because it's a need people genuinely have and people were were downloading and using it.

