00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:30,320
This is kind of like exactly why I love building apps, because it gives me opportunities and things that I couldn't achieve otherwise.

457
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:34,960
And of course, I replied to his email and was like, yeah, let's do something together.

458
00:42:36,320 --> 00:42:48,160
And then we just had a video call and we were discussing, oh yeah, can we maybe have like a little experiment in the app where we ask people to donate their data of their first six weeks of using WONSAG and ask some surveys in the meantime.

459
00:42:50,080 --> 00:43:00,160
And we were really blown away by the results because we could see that on average the social media time was dropping by 57%.

460
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:04,480
I was hoping to see like a statistically significant result, right?

461
00:43:04,720 --> 00:43:12,720
Something like, I don't know, 12% or something like where I could say, okay, it's statistically significant that WONSAG works, but seeing that it's like cut by more.

462
00:43:13,440 --> 00:44:02,080
than 50 percent that was insane and how do you how do you measure that like because you don't have a control right yes by now we actually did some experiments where we have a control group but back then we were looking at how many times you would try to open an app and we would assume that kind of if once it wasn't there all of these attempts would actually lead to a session on social media and then we would like look in the sixth week how many times do you actually open it and that comparison was 57 percent but we were actually able to reproduce that by havinging now we did experiments that had a proper baseline period where we were just recording two weeks of your social media usage and then suddenly the one sec intervention kicks in and we were able to see the same effect.

463
00:44:02,240 --> 00:44:19,920
So kind of like our assumptions from back then regarding the baseline, they were true and like all the experiments that we ran, they were always showing numbers around 57 percent reduction, which is kind of like almost seems like a nature constant of attention that you can steal from someone without noticing it.

464
00:44:20,400 --> 00:44:23,840
Yeah, because you did this original experiment, you got that result.

